1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,779
Imagine you're sitting perfectly still.

2
00:00:03,779 --> 00:00:06,530
But you're moving in at least three ways at once.

3
00:00:07,830 --> 00:00:09,556
First, Earth spins.

4
00:00:09,806 --> 00:00:13,148
Think of a merry-go-round. The edge moves fastest.

5
00:00:13,848 --> 00:00:19,574
On Earth, that's the equator, at about 1,670 km/h.

6
00:00:21,074 --> 00:00:24,226
Nearly twice as fast as a passenger jet.

7
00:00:25,226 --> 00:00:26,925
So why don't we feel it?

8
00:00:27,524 --> 00:00:31,066
On a smooth flight, you can pour a drink without spilling.

9
00:00:31,316 --> 00:00:33,926
Steady motion feels like standing still.

10
00:00:35,226 --> 00:00:37,481
Second, Earth circles the Sun.

11
00:00:37,731 --> 00:00:39,682
Picture running a marathon.

12
00:00:40,282 --> 00:00:43,386
Earth covers that in about a second and a half.

13
00:00:44,586 --> 00:00:47,864
That's more than 100,000 km/h.

14
00:00:49,264 --> 00:00:56,530
Third, the Sun carries us around the centre of the Milky Way, at about 800,000 km/h.

15
00:00:58,030 --> 00:01:01,558
One lap takes around 230 million years.

16
00:01:02,458 --> 00:01:06,686
The last time we were here, the first dinosaurs were just starting out.

17
00:01:08,286 --> 00:01:13,519
So while you watched this, you've travelled about 2,000 km around the Sun.

18
00:01:14,719 --> 00:01:16,554
Not bad for sitting still.
